{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L72"},"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","title":"SegmentStore","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"title":"Stores","anchor":"Stores","generated":true}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore()","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write-through.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, with one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"type":"text","text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss too ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the app moves to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background or terminates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and so is one whose event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every event "},{"code":"DiscoveredEvent.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists, the "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" structs of every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module the program links and the library’s own, or only the "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types in "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is reported as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so a type left out by mistake,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as one that conforms to "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand, shows up."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records after it drops some ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":") is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading back."}]},{"type":"text","text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and waits for a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"reference"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"reference"},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","title":"RecordStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documenta